WEBVTT

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.380
<i>Hisayasu Takemoto, 82 years old.</i>

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.470
HISAYASU TAKEMOTO
FIGHTER, THE BYAKUYA SHIMBUN COMPANY

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.850
<i>At the age of 45, he founded</i>
<i>the "Takemoto Style Combat Kenpo."</i>

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.100
<i>In the 37 years since,</i>

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.230
<i>he has fought more</i>
<i>than 90 unofficial matches,</i>

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.110
<i>and has never lost a single one.</i>

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:32.400
<i>Before long, people started</i>
<i>to call him "God of War."</i>

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.160
Unbelievable!
It's impossible that Takemoto could lose!

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.330
TESAKI AKANO
PRESIDENT, THE BYAKUYA SHIMBUN COMPANY

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.750
Sorry he didn't win.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.120
Who the hell are you?

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.220
I'm so happy!

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.470
MACHIZO INUI
FIGHTER, UMIICHI SECURITIES

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.430
Now I can break humans as much as I like.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:04.600
Kengan matches are... awesome!

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.150
<i>Your fighter is unable to fight anymore.</i>

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.770
Instead of this useless piece of crap,

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.110
hire me as your fighter.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.400
But keep this in mind.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:20.580
If I become the champion, you must
appoint a specific person as chairman.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:21.620
<i>Oh my...</i>

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.830
Mr. Nogi's words have come true.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.170
Considering the high-handed manner,
that man could well be behind it.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.630
RINO KURAYOSHI
REPRESENTATIVE, GOLD PLEASURE GROUP

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.590
REI MIKAZUCHI
FIGHTER, GOLD PLEASURE GROUP

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.800
Give me five seconds.
Wait here, Rino.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:38.640
All I want is your fighter spot.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.180
You don't want to get hurt
by pointlessly resisting, do you?

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.350
<i>In this world, there are some people</i>
<i>who are believed to be geniuses.</i>

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.400
<i>Cosmo Imai, 19 years old.</i>

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.490
<i>At the age of 14, he became</i>
<i>the youngest ever debut in a kengan match.</i>

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.580
<i>Against a man 20cm taller</i>
<i>and 30kg heavier than himself,</i>

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:09.000
<i>he won by ippon,</i>
<i>making his debut a sensation.</i>

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.300
<i>His record in kengan matches is...</i>

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.170
<i>twenty-one wins and no losses.</i>

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.470
<i>There's no doubt about his talent.</i>

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.640
<i>Cosmo Imai is a true genius.</i>

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.320
Python Hold.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.190
You'll be finished soon.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.490
Sweet dreams.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.240
I think you've really underestimated
the kengan match.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.240
COSMO IMAI
A.K.A. "THE KING OF STRANGLERS"

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.500
What's going on?

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:57.420
Oh, no! You've gone too far, Wakatsuki.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.760
Too fragile.
He was broken by one attack.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.010
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI, LONGEST-SERVING FIGHTER
306 WINS 2 LOSSES, HIGHEST WIN RECORD

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:37.980
THE NIGHT BEFORE

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.070
Sorry, Rino.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.200
I kept you waiting for 22 seconds.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:48.870
Raise your head, Rei. I don't mind.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.120
<i>Now you understand, don't you?</i>

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.750
<i>Cheap tricks won't work on us.</i>

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:01.000
That woman is aware of the camera.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:05.760
Rino Kurayoshi... she's a really
tough one to deal with, as usual.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:10.010
-Shall I get rid of her?
-You don't have to. Leave her alone.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.310
We've gained two more spots, after all.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.560
Now our company has six spots,
including yours.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.190
We are fully prepared.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.780
The time has come.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.360
KATSUMASA HAYAMI
CHAIRMAN, TOYO ELECTRIC POWER COMPANY

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:30.450
Get ready, Metsudo Katahara.
Your reign is going to end soon.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.040
KAEDE AKIYAMA
NOGI GROUP

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.040
I can't believe it.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.620
Lihito, how could you lose
all your money at the casino?

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.330
OHMA TOKITA
FIGHTER, YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.130
LIHITO
PRESIDENT & FIGHTER, SH FROZEN STORAGE

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.710
What would you have done
if I hadn't paid it off for you?

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.420
I apologize.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.880
<i>Why am I here?</i>

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.470
-And you, Ohma.
-What?

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.890
I saw you encouraging all those ladies to
sit with you at the casino. Shame on you!

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.890
<i>That wasn't my fault.</i>
<i>They wouldn't leave me alone.</i>

00:05:57.230 --> 00:06:00.270
My point is, you two are at risk
of getting attacked at any moment.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.480
-Please refrain from acting so carelessly.
-Okay, okay.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.530
Well, well. I think that's enough.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.110
KAZUO YAMASHITA
PRESIDENT, YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.160
What the...?

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.750
I see. You're the assassin, aren't you?

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.050
Dodged!

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:25.460
You asshole!

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:32.140
So, your target must be Tokita!

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.980
He used Tokita's leg to jump up on him?

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:42.110
<i>This jerk is...</i>

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.450
You have some nerve.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.360
<i>It's Ohma's turn to attack.</i>

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.700
Ground grappling techniques?

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.500
It's not a bad idea.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:06.210
But unfortunately, you're too light.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.300
He stopped at the last moment!

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:14.350
I'd have landed that blow
if I hadn't noticed. You brat.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.560
A girl?

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.900
You can't mask your gender.
I could tell by your scent.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:27.190
What the hell do you want?

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.280
I want to have a baby with you.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:35.700
What?

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.960
I knew you were strong
as soon as I saw you.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:44.210
I'm Karura. Be my husband.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.210
That's, um...

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:49.460
-A marriage proposal?
-Why is she asking him now?

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.300
My grandpa told me

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.640
that it's the responsibility of the head
of the family to have strong offspring.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:59.430
-Excuse me, miss. Could you explain--
-Let's make babies together!

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:00.680
Hello, are you ignoring me?

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.730
<i>They were all very confused</i>

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.480
<i>by her sudden and baffling</i>
<i>marriage proposal.</i>

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.940
<i>But the one who felt most confused was...</i>

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:12.860
<i>this man.</i>

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.160
<i>Babies? Husband?</i>

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.950
<i>Me? With this girl?</i>

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.660
<i>What the hell is she talking about?</i>

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:24.460
<i>Wow, even Ohma is shocked,</i>
<i>and he's usually so cool!</i>

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.750
Come on, let's make some babies together!
Children that are yours and mine!

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:31.510
Our children will undoubtedly
become the greatest ever warriors!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.840
Let's get married right now!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.810
Wait, Ohma! Where are you going?

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:49.400
I think he's running away because
the situation got too much for him.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:50.780
He's acting like a kid.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:52.940
There you are, Karura.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:55.860
Don't wander around on your own.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.120
<i>Those guys are from...</i>

00:08:58.320 --> 00:08:59.200
<i>the Kure Family.</i>

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:00.990
REICHI KURE & HOLLIS KURE
KURE FAMILY

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.620
-What would you do if you got lost?
-Let's get back.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.210
Grandpa is worried about you.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.170
<i>I don't like the nasty way</i>
<i>they're looking at us.</i>

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.090
<i>It's like we're their prey.</i>

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.420
We're very sorry one
of our family bothered you.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.890
No problem at all.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.970
-His name...
-What?

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.560
KARURA KURE
KURE FAMILY

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.060
What's his name?

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.520
The name of your future husband?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.600
It's Seaweed Head Monster.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.730
His name is Ohma Tokita.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:31.400
Ohma Tokita.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.860
It's not sea eel, okay?

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.610
He's Ohma.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:40.700
Tell Ohma
that I want to see him again.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.950
I guess he won't want to though.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:47.250
Welcome back, Karura.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.290
HORIO KURE, ERIO KURE, RAIAN KURE
KURE FAMILY

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.630
-Did you enjoy your expedition?
-Grandpa.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.010
I have...

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.010
I have a crush on someone.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.970
What? That's...

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:05.770
-That's nice, honey.
-Yeah.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.980
We'll talk more about it later.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.610
-Go and have dinner now.
-Okay!

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.610
The kid's taken an interest in boys!

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.200
Stop teasing, Raian.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:23.120
What's going on?

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:28.040
His name is Ohma Tokita,
he represents Yamashita Corporation.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:32.460
Oh... he was the one
I saw with Lihito at the match.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:37.470
I see, so it's him.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:41.180
That son of a bitch!

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:46.350
Karura's still in high school.
How could he hit on her?

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.440
That goddamn moron!

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.480
My sides hurt.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.940
You know what to do, right?

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.190
Keep an eye on Ohma Tokita.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:59.490
If he comes near Karura again,

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:02.780
erase him completely from this world!

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.990
Don't leave so much as
one of his hairs behind!

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.040
Hey, old man.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:13.040
You're losing control of yourself.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:17.880
<i>Inside the Kure, a demon resides.</i>

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:24.220
<i>Daybreak has arrived.</i>

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:28.390
We will soon arrive at the site
where the decisive battle will take place.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.770
I believe you've already chosen...

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:35.110
METSUDO KATAHARA, GOVERNOR OF DAINIPPON
BANK & KENGAN ASSOCIATION CHAIRMAN

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.480
...the fighter in whom
you will entrust your destiny.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:45.870
<i>The bloody battle between men of valour</i>
<i>is finally about to begin.</i>

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.120
<i>I welcome this grim setting.</i>

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.330
GANRYU ISLAND

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:52.120
<i>It is the perfect place</i>
<i>to fight to the death!</i>

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.590
<i>Okay, I must prepare myself.</i>

00:11:55.790 --> 00:12:00.840
<i>Whatever happens from now on,</i>
<i>I will not lose my cool!</i>

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:18.690
GANRYU ISLAND HOTEL

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:22.200
VENUE OF THE DRAWING
OF PAIRINGS FOR THE TOURNAMENT

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:25.660
FOR THE PARTICIPANTS OF
THE LIFE-OR-DEATH TOURNAMENT

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:29.290
KIRIMI TAKAKAZE

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.290
TOMARI TOHGO

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.290
Y. DAZAI
MUJI TV NETWORK

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.290
Do you know who he is?

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.860
TAKASHI HASHIDA, SENTORY CHAIRMAN
KOHNO AKIO, NENTENDO PRESIDENT

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.740
He's the new face
they've been talking about.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:42.550
<i>I feel completely out of place.</i>

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.220
JUZO MAGATANI
PRESIDENT, MAGATANIEN

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:46.720
Why are we still waiting?
Come on, shake a leg!

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:53.850
KATSUMASA HAYAMI
CHAIRMAN, TOYO ELECTRIC POWER COMPANY

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:57.610
<i>Am I really meant to compete</i>
<i>with these eminent people?</i>

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:00.400
<i>Is that Ken?</i>

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:01.730
KEN OHYA
GINOKUNIYA BOOKSHOP

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:02.690
Hi, Ken.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:09.280
<i>Why is Ken with Mr. Hayami?</i>

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.660
I'm expecting a favorable response
from you, Mr. Ohya.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:17.500
It would be better for you
not to choose the wrong side.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.090
Thank you very much
for your kind advice.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.970
What's wrong with Ken?

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:27.550
Oh dear, you're Mr. Yamashita,
the man everyone's talking about.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.970
Oh, President Yoshitake.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.180
YOSHIRO YOSHITAKE
PRESIDENT, YOSHITAKE REAL ESTATE

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.310
It's been a while. I didn't think it was
possible to come here by total fluke.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.440
And Lihito.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:41.940
You're the president and the fighter?
Don't make me laugh.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:48.200
I've found the strongest fighter
of you all, you'll be no match for him!

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:53.200
You know what?
You've got the wrong idea.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.040
It's been a long time
since I worked for you.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:59.170
You're not my employer anymore,
you're not anything to me.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.790
We are complete strangers to each other.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:06.470
Stop acting like the top man
or I'll rip your body apart, my ex-boss.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.680
You're just showing off!

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:13.720
-He ran away.
-Oh my...

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.060
It's nice you're all good friends.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:18.100
RINO KURAYOSHI
REPRESENTATIVE. GOLD PLEASURE GROUP

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.270
Wow, Rino!

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.610
<i>What an outrageously</i>
<i>beautiful lady she is.</i>

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.270
Attention, please.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.990
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.740
<i>Metsudo Katahara is here.</i>

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:32.740
<i>Hmm... Is that Chairman Nogi?</i>

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:34.830
HIDEKI NOGI
CHAIRMAN, NOGI GROUP

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:37.040
He looks fired up.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:40.420
I've never seen Mr. Nogi
with such a serious look on his face.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:46.170
No wonder.
His company will be finished if he loses.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:47.260
What?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:51.340
Excuse me, Rino.
What do you mean by "finished"?

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:56.520
Well, if the promoter, Mr. Nogi,
loses in this tournament,

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.850
Nogi Group will be dissolved immediately.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.560
-Dissolved?
-Dissolved?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.980
<i>Bankruptcy, in other words?</i>
<i>This is terrible!</i>

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:09.150
<i>I don't want to lose my job at my age.</i>

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:16.540
<i>But wait. Remember the debt</i>
<i>I was forced to bear? Five billion yen.</i>

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.960
<i>I might be able to cancel</i>
<i>the contract, right?</i>

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:23.290
<i>Yes, the slate will be wiped clean</i>
<i>if the company goes belly up.</i>

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:28.760
<i>As I also have some savings,</i>
<i>I think I'll be able to figure a way out.</i>

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.800
I heard from Mr. Nogi...

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:34.800
that you two bet your lives
on the tournament.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:36.680
What? Our lives?

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:40.770
He said that you managed to make
the five billion yen entry fee

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:43.980
by taking out a mortgage
on all of your private assets.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:44.940
What?

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:50.820
You'll be literally penniless if you lose.
You have such indomitable spirit.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.030
<i>What? Didn't he just lend the money to me?</i>

00:15:55.660 --> 00:16:01.210
<i>If we lose the tournament does this</i>
<i>mean my life is going to fall apart?</i>

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:05.380
<i>We are in the same boat, Yamashita.</i>

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.260
<i>Jeez... I think I have no hope left.</i>

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.510
You must all be ready by now.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:19.140
We are now going to determine
the tournament match-ups.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.270
KENGAN ASSOCIATION

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.350
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.860
-We must win at any cost, Kazuo.
-Oh my...

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:26.830
DAINIPPON BANK

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.110
Dainippon Bank has already been placed

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:31.940
in the last game of the first round.

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:35.950
I'm sure all of you
will already be aware of this.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.410
The game you should
pay attention to is this one.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:44.540
The battle with the strongest fighter,
Agito Kanoh, or Fang of Metsudo,

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.920
is the one you must try to avoid.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:48.290
True.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:53.010
We don't want our fighters to have to
fight a fully fit Fang in the first round.

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.350
Now, let's get started.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.390
We're going to use this.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.810
-What is it?
-What's that?

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:05.390
SUKIZO URITA
PRESIDENT, PENASONIC CORP

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:06.560
What is that machine, sir?

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:10.270
I'll demonstrate how it works
so it's easier for you to understand.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:13.190
Here, here, here...

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:14.530
And here.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.910
That's it.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:23.660
The higher your number, the sooner you
can choose your position in the match-up.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.000
MAKOTO YANAGI
UNITED CLOTHING

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.420
SHUNKA HIYAMA
WAKASA LIFE INSURANCE

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:29.540
I'm not using any machine you've
brought in. You could cheat us!

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:32.880
I've very kindly made
these arrangements for you.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.970
Stop complaining and obey my rule!

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:40.470
Well, who wants to go first?

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:41.600
I do!

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.560
-Well...
-I'll go first!

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.770
What about the new face, Mr. Yamashita?

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:51.940
<i>No!</i>

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:56.400
Okay! Come on, Yamashita.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:59.450
<i>What did I do to deserve this?</i>

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.620
Now! Push the button.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.330
<i>Too fast. I have no choice.</i>

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:11.040
<i>I'll just push the button at random.</i>

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:14.800
<i>Wait. What's this?</i>

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:17.550
<i>Is it... okay?</i>

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.510
You did it, Yamashita.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:29.230
You got 989,086,296.

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:33.020
-Wow.
-We've started with a huge number.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:37.400
You're very likely to go
first in the match-ups.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.660
Huh? Ah, y... yes.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:45.540
<i>No one noticed that the speed</i>
<i>slowed down strangely.</i>

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.160
<i>Was it cheating?</i>

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:52.290
<i>Well, I guess it's okay.</i>
<i>I'll keep quiet unless someone notices.</i>

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.630
Good! I'll follow Kazuo's lead!

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:01.510
-Only three digits.
-<i>He should have paid closer attention.</i>

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.720
<i>I can't get the exact number I want.</i>

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:11.190
<i>But all I have to do is to focus on</i>
<i>the far-left digit.</i>

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:15.110
Another big number!

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.200
AKIRA NISHIHONJI

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.200
SHION SORYUIN

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:25.410
All right, now we know everyone's score.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:29.160
Let's start with Yamashita Corporation
as they got the top score.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.580
Yes!

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.630
Which one will you choose?

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.250
<i>Well, um...</i>

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:40.380
<i>The main thing to avoid</i>
<i>is being in the same block as Fang.</i>

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:41.590
Excuse me, sir.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:43.590
Have you decided yet?

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:47.970
Yes... well, then...
I'd like to choose that position.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:51.350
Number eight in the fourth game.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.560
YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:57.650
<i>It's obvious that he'd choose the opposite</i>
<i>block to the one with Fang of Metsudo.</i>

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.990
<i>He'll also be able to get a feel for</i>
<i>the tournament from the first three games.</i>

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:02.990
MASAHIKO OHTA
PRESIDENT, UNDER MOUNT INC

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:05.490
<i>The earlier game will help</i>
<i>his fighter maintain his motivation</i>

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.080
<i>What an excellent choice.</i>

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.460
<i>I was rushed into choosing it at random.</i>

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:16.090
<i>I hope Ohma will be all right with this.</i>

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.550
All right.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.590
We have completed
the tournament match-ups.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.550
You are dismissed!

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:26.260
<i>Was it really a good choice?</i>

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.430
Finally, it's time
to kick off the festival!

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:30.180
JUN SEKIBAYASHI
FIGHTER, GANDAI

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:31.930
Alrighty! I've waited so long for this!

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:33.810
SAW PAING YOROIZUKA
FIGHTER, VILLAGE OF DAWN

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.190
I've been feeling the urge to fight.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.610
I note you're as noisy as always.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:40.690
GAOLAN WONGSAWAT
FIGHTER, YAZU TRADING

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.650
Why is a guy like you interested in
this tournament anyway, Saw Paing?

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.070
You're asking me why?
What a silly question!

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.950
It's obvious, Gaolan.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:52.410
A man should talk with his fist, right?

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:55.210
-Yes!
-So annoying.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.460
In this tournament,
no one can be underestimated.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.500
KEIZABURO SAWADA
FIGHTER, MURDER MUSIC

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.760
But I'm pretty sure that
I'm going to end up champion.

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:04.800
What are you doing? So creepy!

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.760
RYO INABA
FIGHTER, PENASONIC CORPORATION

00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:10.140
Well, well... it's going
to get really tough now.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:11.970
SEN HATSUMI
FIGHTER, NOGI GROUP

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.020
Actually, I'm not
the kind of guy to work hard.

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:19.230
I'm finally going to fight with you,
Ohma Tokita.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.190
SETSUNA KIRYU
FIGHTER, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.780
I won't let anyone get in my way.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.360
I'll annihilate them.
I'm going to kill them all.

00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:27.780
RAIAN KURE
FIGHTER, UNDER MOUNT INC

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:31.160
<i>This is the secret side</i>
<i>of the Japanese economy.</i>

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.540
<i>It's a world of demonic war,</i>
<i>full of ambition and conspiracy,</i>

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:38.040
<i>where people struggle for power.</i>

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.130
<i>This is a proxy war...</i>

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:44.220
<i>using an extremely simple tool: violence.</i>

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:49.890
<i>Now, 32 companies and their fighters</i>
<i>are aiming for the top position.</i>

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:53.270
<i>Who is the strongest?</i>

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:56.060
AGITO KANOH, A.K.A. "FANG OF METSUDO"
THE EMPEROR OF KENGAN MATCHES

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:02.440
<i>I wonder if I made a right choice.</i>

00:22:02.690 --> 00:22:07.070
<i>I don't think they'll give me</i>
<i>another chance, though...</i>

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:19.660
We'll do it, Kazuo Yamashita.

00:22:19.790 --> 00:22:22.170
OHMA TOKITA, FIGHTER, YAMASHITA CORP.
NIKO TOKITA'S SUCCESSOR

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:24.090
Yes...

00:22:26.420 --> 00:22:27.380
We will!

00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:32.970
<i>Finally, the Kengan Life-or-Death</i>
<i>Tournament is about to start.</i>

00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:35.980
THE KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH
TOURNAMENT BEGINS

00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:06.900
PREVIEW

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:07.940
<i>The wait is over.</i>

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:11.360
<i>The Kengan Life-or-Death</i>
<i>Tournament has begun.</i>

00:24:11.530 --> 00:24:13.990
<i>It's fists versus</i>
<i>ground grappling techniques.</i>

00:24:14.070 --> 00:24:17.700
<i>I am, I am, I am...</i>
<i>stronger than you!</i>

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:19.240
Next episode: "The Battle Begins"

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:20.960
Subtitle translation by
Hinako Someno
